35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The taster forms show people fear a whole-year commitment. The ledger shows fixed costs are high.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The treasurer spent six hours a month chasing individual payments. The ledger confirms fixed costs dominate.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,A quarter of members do two-thirds of the work. The same nine people set up and lock up.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,Turnout dropped a third after door charges. Quiet members feel uneasy about per-event costs.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,A third of renewals needed reminders. Mid-year joiners required hand-worked calculations. Cash flow is messy.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin If chasing payments takes six hours, activity-based charging is impossible for us.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,@Asuka Correct. The administrative load is the killer. We need a simple collection method.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shunichi If we charge per event, the quiet members will feel even more alienated.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan Agreed. The hesitation is real. We need a structure that feels like belonging, not a transaction.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,@Benjamin The bank statements show people want to spread payments. A flat fee might be too high upfront.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,Tiered membership might work. It lets people choose their level of involvement without hidden costs.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Tiered membership simplifies collection. One fee per tier, no chasing individual events.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,But does it address the workload imbalance? The same nine people still do the heavy lifting.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"It might. If the lower tier is for socials only, the higher tier for active participation, it clarifies expectations.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"It reduces the mid-year calculation nightmare. If they pick a tier, the math is done.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I am leaning towards Tiered Membership. It respects the newcomers' fear of commitment.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I support it. It is the only model that keeps the treasurer sane.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I have concerns about the workload, but it is better than the current chaos.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,It removes the hesitation. People know exactly what they are signing up for.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"It solves the cash flow issue. Predictable income, predictable costs. I am in.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
